{"type":"text","timestamp":1788347820448,"sessionID":"ses_f9e2d9b94ffe0d28psipaZ0tQy","part":{"id":"prt_061d5f479001wmkFhaBy37B4o4","messageID":"msg_061d57ee4001xgMJlZPrJuwiGk","sessionID":"ses_f9e2d9b94ffe0d28psipaZ0tQy","type":"text","text":"I've now thoroughly reviewed all the materials. Let me perform the systematic static review against the CANNBench contract and all 20 case routes.\n\n## Static Review of candidate.py\n\n**Category 1: Syntax compliance** (inside `@asc2.jit`)\n- No `print`, `break`, `continue`, `lambda`, `try/except`, `import`, nested functions, `global`, `return`, `math.*`, `range()` — all clear.\n- Variables initialized before use, no conditional-only definitions — clear.\n- Uses `asc2.range()` not `range()` — clear.\n\n**Category 2: Pinned-v2 API correctness**\n- `asc2.global_tensor(ptr, [size])` — 1-D, matches contract.\n- `asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])` — exact pattern match.\n- `asc2.copy_out(tile, out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])` — exact pattern match.\n- `asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(), unroll_factor=2)` — correct, no `parallel`/`gm_barrier`.\n- `asc2.abs`, `asc2.exp`, `asc2.where`, comparison `xf >= 0.0`, arithmetic `+ - * /` — all in the allowed op list.\n- `asc.GlobalAddress` pointers, `int` sizes, `asc.ConstExpr[int]` tile_size — correct types.\n- Launch `kernel[cores](...)` with `cores = min(72, num_tiles)`, no stream — correct.\n- No asc v1 APIs (`GlobalTensor`, `data_copy`, `set_flag`, `TPosition`, `BUFFER_NUM`) — clear.\n\n**Category 3: Scalar ordering** — All scalars on RIGHT: `two_w + 1.0`, `neg_num + 2.0`. Tile-tile ops (`w * w`, `pos_num / pos_den`, `xf * th`) are fine. Clear.\n\n**Category 4: dtype promotion** — `xf = x.to(asc.float32)` for f16/bf16/f32; `y.to(x.dtype)` casts back. Clear.\n\n**Category 5: UB budget** — 15 visible f32 tiles + 1 bool tile at TILE=1024: `15 * 4 * 1024 * 2 * 1.6 = 196,608 B < 253,952 B`. `asc2.where`/comparison dest: `1024 * 4 = 4096 B`, `4096 % 256 = 0`. Clear.\n\n**Category 6: Numerical stability** — Uses the exact cancellation-free identity from task.md: `w = exp(-|x|)` (never positive arg), no `log(1+tiny)`, no catastrophic cancellation. IEEE special values (inf/-inf/NaN) propagate correctly: x=+inf → y=+inf; x=-inf → y=NaN (matches golden IEEE); x=NaN → NaN; x=0 → y=0. Clear.\n\n**Category 7: Anti-cheat** — All numerics in `@asc2.jit`; torch only for `empty_like`, `numel()`, `is_contiguous()`, `contiguous()`; no torch compute ops; `ensure_npu_platform()` first. Clear.\n\n**Category 8: All 20 case routes** — Single code path (flatten-1D, grid-stride, tail via `real_shape`). Every case has numel ≥ ~1M so cores=72 always saturated. Covers: f16 (1,4,7,10,14,17), f32 (2,5,8,11,13,15,18,20), bf16 (3,6,9,12,16,19); ranks 1D-5D; non-power-of-2 shapes (1023, 1009, 1021, 8193, 1000003); special values (inf/-inf in 12, NaN in 13, all-zero in 14, max-f16 range in 10/17). All route through the same kernel. Clear.\n\n**Category 9: Module shape** — Imports correct (`torch`, `asc`, `asc2`, `ensure_npu_platform`); one `@asc2.jit` kernel; one public callable `mish(x: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor`; `size==0` early return; bare `@asc2.jit` (no `always_compile`). Clear.\n\nNo issues found. The candidate is correct as-is. Let me run the syntax check.","time":{"start":1788347806841,"end":1788347820446}}}
